description:
In repos/activity-api/src/routes/execution-traces.ts, fix the inverted default projection on the execution-traces LIST handler. Line 732 currently reads exactly these two lines:

    const summaryProjection =
      fieldsParam === 'summary' || detailParam !== 'true';

Change the second line to read exactly:

      fieldsParam === 'summary' || detailParam === 'false';

That is the entire change: replace the operator and literal `!== 'true'` with `=== 'false'`. Do not modify anything else. Rationale, which the file already documents in the comment block immediately above lines 718-731: that comment promises "The DEFAULT projection is left WIDE and unchanged - many autonomous consumers (development-vessel resolvers, boredom-vessel) read metadata, composition_chain, failure_mode, and input/output_impulse_shapes off this list response, so narrowing the default would silently break them." But detailParam is c.req.query('detail'), which is undefined when a caller omits it, and undefined !== 'true' evaluates TRUE, so summaryProjection defaults to true and every unadorned caller silently receives the NARROW projection. The code does the opposite of what its own comment guarantees. After the change, the wide projection is the default and narrowing remains opt-in via ?fields=summary or ?detail=false, exactly as documented.

Do NOT touch the selectFields ternary at line 887 - its wide branch already correctly lists failure_mode, metadata, output_impulse_shapes and input_impulse_shapes. Do NOT touch the limit clamp at line 736; that is a separate defect and bundling it will cause this patch to be rejected.

Verified live before filing: GET /v2/activities/execution-traces?limit=3 returns rows with a failure_mode_type scalar and no metadata field, while the identical request with &detail=true returns the same rows carrying full failure_mode and metadata objects. The data is present in the table; only the default projection hides it.

